{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":704,"final_message_hash":"sha256:0a29702fec7f788491a2407477e44de851d2c0b9fb6dfd90c3e5c504ba4cfd2b","final_message_inline":"Perfect! All contract checks are passing. The fix was straightforward:\n\n**The Problem:** After the vendor bump to slugify 2.0.0, the API signature changed from `slugify(text, separator)` to `slugify(text, options)`. The old code was calling `slugify(title, \"-\")`, which treated the string as an options object, causing the function to fall back to the default underscore separator.\n\n**The Solution:** Updated `pageSlug()` in `src/pages.ts` to use the new API correctly: `slugify(title, { separator: \"-\", lower: true })`, which explicitly sets the separator to hyphens and lowercases the output.\n\nAll tests pass and page slugs are back to their original hyphenated format, preserving existing links.\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:95d8d757d798c6f2fd9df03ddf686bf60075a483dc7227736592ef45c0203986","hook_ms":3,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":32134929791,"prev":"sha256:ce6efeefcd944eec6c1e5da86320f5a5423dc3c2ca27cb51ae465b4f5277919d","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":33,"session":"60fc0966-c175-4011-b3a3-56303e83b9cf","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T15:25:57.984Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
